{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"886","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Maximum Element"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"One day Petya was solving a very interesting problem. But although he used many optimization techniques, his solution still got Time limit exceeded verdict. Petya conducted a thorough analysis of his program and found out that his function for finding maximum element in an array of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" positive integers was too slow. Desperate, Petya decided to use a somewhat unexpected optimization using parameter "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":", so now his function contains the following code:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nint fast_max(int n, int a[]) { \n    int ans = 0;\n    int offset = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i)\n        if (ans < a[i]) {\n            ans = a[i];\n            offset = 0;\n        } else {\n            offset = offset + 1;\n            if (offset == k)\n                return ans;\n        }\n    return ans;\n}\n"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"That way the function iteratively checks array elements, storing the intermediate maximum, and if after "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" consecutive iterations that maximum has not changed, it is returned as the answer."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now Petya is interested in fault rate of his function. He asked you to find the number of permutations of integers from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" such that the return value of his function on those permutations is not equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":". Since this number could be very big, output the answer modulo "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"109 + 7"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n, k ≤ 106"},{"kind":"text","text":"), separated by a space — the length of the permutations and the parameter "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output the answer to the problem modulo "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"109 + 7"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"22\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"84\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Permutations from second example: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[4, 1, 2, 3, 5]"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[4, 1, 3, 2, 5]"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[4, 2, 1, 3, 5]"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[4, 2, 3, 1, 5]"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[4, 3, 1, 2, 5]"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[4, 3, 2, 1, 5]"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"886E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/886/problem/E"}